.SS "void p4est_connectivity_coordinates_canonicalize (\fBp4est_connectivity_t\fP * conn, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP treeid, const \fBp4est_qcoord_t\fP coords[], \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP * treeid_out, \fBp4est_qcoord_t\fP coords_out[])"

.PP
Determine the owning tree for a coordinate and transform it there\&. On a boundary between trees, different coordinate systems meet\&. A coordinate on a tree boundary face or corner generated from the perspective of a specific tree may be transformed into any other touching tree's coordinate system and still refer to the same point in the mesh\&.
.PP
To uniquely identify a coordinate, this function identifies the lowest numbered tree touching this coordinate and transforms the coordinates into that system\&. The result can be used e\&. g\&. in topology hash tables\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconn\fP A valid connectivity\&. 
.br
\fItreeid\fP The original tree index for this coordinate tuple\&. 
.br
\fIcoords\fP A valid coordinate 2-tuple relative to \fItreeid\fP\&. 
.br
\fItreeid_out\fP The lowest tree index touching the coordinate\&. 
.br
\fIcoords_out\fP The input coordinates, if necessary after transformation into the system of the lowest numbered tree, returned in \fItreeid_out\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

