.SS "\fBp4est_connectivity_t\fP* p4est_connectivity_read_inp (const char * filename)"

.PP
Create a \fBp4est\fP connectivity from an ABAQUS input file\&. This utility function reads a basic ABAQUS file supporting element type with the prefix C2D4, CPS4, and S4 in 2D and of type C3D8 reading them as bilinear quadrilateral and trilinear hexahedral trees respectively\&.
.PP
A basic 2D mesh is given below\&. The \fC*Node\fP section gives the vertex number and x, y, and z components for each vertex\&. The \fC*Element\fP section gives the 4 vertices in 2D (8 vertices in 3D) of each element in counter clockwise order\&. So in 2D the nodes are given as: 
.PP
.nf
4                     3
 +-------------------+
 |                   |
 |                   |
 |                   |
 |                   |
 |                   |
 |                   |
 +-------------------+
1                     2

.fi
.PP
 and in 3D they are given as: 
.PP
.nf
8                     7
 +---------------------+
 |\                    |\
 | \                   | \
 |  \                  |  \
 |   \                 |   \
 |   5+---------------------+6
 |    |                |    |
 +----|----------------+    |
 4\   |               3 \   |
   \  |                  \  |
    \ |                   \ |
     \|                    \|
      +---------------------+
      1                     2

.fi
.PP
 
.PP
.nf
*Heading
 box\&.inp
*Node
1,  -5, -5, 0
2,   5, -5, 0
3,   5,  5, 0
4,  -5,  5, 0
5,   0, -5, 0
6,   5,  0, 0
7,   0,  5, 0
8,  -5,  0, 0
9,   1, -1, 0
10,  0,  0, 0
11, -2,  1, 0
*Element, type=CPS4, ELSET=Surface1
1,  1, 10, 11, 8
2,  3, 10, 9,  6
3,  9, 10, 1,  5
4,  7,  4, 8, 11
5, 11, 10, 3,  7
6,  2,  6, 9,  5

.fi
.PP
.PP
This function reads a mesh from \fIfilename\fP and returns an associated \fBp4est\fP connectivity\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfilename\fP file to read the connectivity from
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
an allocated connectivity associated with the mesh in \fIfilename\fP or NULL if an error occurred\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int p4est_connectivity_read_inp_stream (FILE * stream, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP * num_vertices, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP * num_trees, double * vertices, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP * tree_to_vertex)"

.PP
Read an ABAQUS input file from a file stream\&. This utility function reads a basic ABAQUS file supporting element type with the prefix C2D4, CPS4, and S4 in 2D and of type C3D8 reading them as bilinear quadrilateral and trilinear hexahedral trees respectively\&.
.PP
A basic 2D mesh is given below\&. The \fC*Node\fP section gives the vertex number and x, y, and z components for each vertex\&. The \fC*Element\fP section gives the 4 vertices in 2D (8 vertices in 3D) of each element in counter clockwise order\&. So in 2D the nodes are given as: 
.PP
.nf
4                     3
 +-------------------+
 |                   |
 |                   |
 |                   |
 |                   |
 |                   |
 |                   |
 +-------------------+
1                     2

.fi
.PP
 and in 3D they are given as: 
.PP
.nf
8                     7
 +---------------------+
 |\                    |\
 | \                   | \
 |  \                  |  \
 |   \                 |   \
 |   5+---------------------+6
 |    |                |    |
 +----|----------------+    |
 4\   |               3 \   |
   \  |                  \  |
    \ |                   \ |
     \|                    \|
      +---------------------+
      1                     2

.fi
.PP
 
.PP
.nf
*Heading
 box\&.inp
*Node
1,  -5, -5, 0
2,   5, -5, 0
3,   5,  5, 0
4,  -5,  5, 0
5,   0, -5, 0
6,   5,  0, 0
7,   0,  5, 0
8,  -5,  0, 0
9,   1, -1, 0
10,  0,  0, 0
11, -2,  1, 0
*Element, type=CPS4, ELSET=Surface1
1,  1, 10, 11, 8
2,  3, 10, 9,  6
3,  9, 10, 1,  5
4,  7,  4, 8, 11
5, 11, 10, 3,  7
6,  2,  6, 9,  5

.fi
.PP
.PP
This code can be called two ways\&. The first, when \fCvertex==NULL\fP and \fCtree_to_vertex==NULL\fP, is used to count the number of trees and vertices in the connectivity to be generated by the \fC\fP\&.inp mesh in the \fIstream\fP\&. The second, when \fCvertices!=NULL\fP and \fCtree_to_vertex!=NULL\fP, fill \fCvertices\fP and \fCtree_to_vertex\fP\&. In this case \fCnum_vertices\fP and \fCnum_trees\fP need to be set to the maximum number of entries allocated in \fCvertices\fP and \fCtree_to_vertex\fP\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstream\fP file stream to read the connectivity from 
.br
\fInum_vertices\fP the number of vertices in the connectivity 
.br
\fInum_trees\fP the number of trees in the connectivity 
.br
\fIvertices\fP the list of \fCvertices\fP of the connectivity 
.br
\fItree_to_vertex\fP the \fCtree_to_vertex\fP map of the connectivity
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
0 if successful and nonzero if not 
.RE
.PP

