.SS "void p4est_connectivity_reorder (sc_MPI_Comm comm, int k, \fBp4est_connectivity_t\fP * conn, \fBp4est_connect_type_t\fP ctype)"

.PP
Reorder a connectivity using METIS\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This function is only available if configured successfully \fC--with-metis\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
This function takes a connectivity \fIconn\fP and a parameter \fIk\fP, which will typically be the number of processes, and reorders the trees such that if every processes is assigned (num_trees / k) trees, the communication volume will be minimized\&. This is intended for use with connectivities that contain a large number of trees\&. This should be done BEFORE a \fBp4est\fP is created using the connectivity\&. This is done in place: any data structures that use indices to refer to trees before this procedure will be invalid\&. Note that this routine calls metis and not parmetis because the connectivity is copied on every process\&. A communicator is required because I'm not positive that metis is deterministic\&. \fIctype\fP determines when an edge exist between two trees in the dual graph used by metis in the reordering\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcomm\fP MPI communicator\&. 
.br
\fIk\fP if k > 0, the number of pieces metis will use to guide the reordering; if k = 0, the number of pieces will be determined from the MPI communicator\&. 
.br
\fIconn\fP connectivity that will be reordered\&. 
.br
\fIctype\fP determines when an edge exists in the dual graph of the connectivity structure\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "sc_array_t* p4est_connectivity_reorder_newid (sc_MPI_Comm comm, int k, \fBp4est_connectivity_t\fP * conn, \fBp4est_connect_type_t\fP ctype, sc_array_t * newid)"

.PP
Reorder a connectivity using METIS\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This function is only available if configured successfully \fC--with-metis\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
This is the same form as \fBp4est_connectivity_reorder\fP but it takes an initialized sc array \fInewid\fP as extra argument\&. In this way, the users can map old indices to new indices in the case it is necessary (for instance to retrieve high-order nodes previously stored in an array with old indices)\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcomm\fP MPI communicator\&. 
.br
\fIk\fP if k > 0, the number of pieces metis will use to guide the reordering; if k = 0, the number of pieces will be determined from the MPI communicator\&. 
.br
\fIconn\fP connectivity that will be reordered\&. 
.br
\fIctype\fP determines when an edge exists in the dual graph of the connectivity structure\&. 
.br
\fInewid\fP array that maps old tree indices to new ones\&. newid has to be an sc_array and it has to be initialized (non-NULL) with element size of size_t (using sc_array_new (sizeof (size_t)))\&. Input length arbitrary, output length modified\&. 
.RE
.PP

