.SS "\fBp4est_connectivity_shared_t\fP* p4est_connectivity_share (\fBp4est_connectivity_t\fP * conn_in, int root, sc_MPI_Comm comm)"

.PP
Take a connectivity on a single rank and share it with MPI3\&. If MPI shared windows are not found at configure time, this function calls \fBp4est_connectivity_bcast\fP instead and wraps its result in the result\&. The function is collective over the communicator passed\&.
.PP
This function is only well defined for an intranode communicator\&. Before calling it, the input connectivity may be made available on the \fIroot\fP rank using \fBp4est_connectivity_bcast\fP with a surrounding communicator that contains one root process of every node\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconn_in\fP For the root process a valid connectivity to be shared by MPI3\&. This function takes ownership of this argument, so it must no longer be used\&. For all other processes it must be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIroot\fP The rank of the process that provides the input connectivity\&. Must be legal wrt\&. \fIcomm\fP\&. 
.br
\fIcomm\fP When configured with MPI3 enabled, this intranode communicator must permit MPI3 windows\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new connectivity object stores all data of the input \fIconn\fP in MPI3 shared windows\&. Must be freed by \fBp4est_connectivity_shared_destroy\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

